Hello and welcome back to our Business English podcast. We're really happy you're here with

3
00:00:18,960 --> 00:00:24,820
us today. If this is your first time listening, welcome. And if you're a regular listener,

4
00:00:24,820 --> 00:00:27,680
thanks for coming back. My name is Marco.

5
00:00:27,680 --> 00:00:31,360
And I'm Erica. Thanks for spending a few minutes of your day learning English with

6
00:00:31,360 --> 00:00:36,960
us. Let me ask you something right away. Have you ever wanted to talk about salary

7
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:40,520
at work, but your mind went completely blank?

8
00:00:40,520 --> 00:00:44,320
You knew what you wanted to say, but you didn't know how to say it in English.

9
00:00:44,320 --> 00:00:49,800
Yeah, maybe you wanted to ask about pay during a job interview, or maybe you wanted to talk

10
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:51,980
to your manager about a raise.

11
00:00:51,980 --> 00:00:57,240
But instead of speaking up, you stayed quiet because you were worried about sounding rude,

12
00:00:57,240 --> 00:00:59,840
awkward, or unprofessional.

13
00:00:59,840 --> 00:01:01,960
That actually happens a lot.

14
00:01:01,960 --> 00:01:06,160
Just last week, one of our listeners sent us a message saying she accepted a job

15
00:01:06,160 --> 00:01:12,080
offer without negotiating the salary, not because she didn't care, but because she was afraid

16
