of saying the wrong thing in English.

17
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:18,960
And that's exactly why today's episode is so important.

18
00:01:18,960 --> 00:01:25,040
Today we're talking about how to talk about salary at work in English, politely, professionally,

19
00:01:25,040 --> 00:01:26,920
and confidently.

20
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:31,160
Salary conversations are stressful for everyone, even native speakers.

21
00:01:31,160 --> 00:01:36,840
So for English learners, they're especially tricky because money has hidden cultural rules.

22
00:01:36,840 --> 00:01:38,340
Exactly.

23
00:01:38,340 --> 00:01:41,480
One wrong phrase can make you sound too direct.

24
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:44,860
Another phrase can sound emotional or even aggressive.

25
00:01:44,860 --> 00:01:48,160
And sometimes people won't tell you that you said something wrong.

26
00:01:48,160 --> 00:01:50,560
They'll just feel uncomfortable.

27
00:01:50,560 --> 00:01:54,160
So in this episode, we're going to help you avoid those problems.

28
00:01:54,160 --> 00:01:58,840
By the end, you'll know how to ask about salary without sounding rude, how to talk

29
00:01:58,840 --> 00:02:05,040
about raises and compensation like a professional and how to avoid common mistakes English learners

30
00:02:05,040 --> 00:02:08,000
make when talking about money at work.

31
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:10,640
Before we jump in, quick question for you.

32
00:02:10,640 --> 00:02:14,880
