00:30:37,960 --> 00:30:42,400
The manager didn't argue, but the conversation became very tense.

486
00:30:42,400 --> 00:30:43,480
Exactly.

487
00:30:43,480 --> 00:30:47,720
The idea might be valid, but the language is too strong.

488
00:30:47,720 --> 00:30:50,480
Now let's look at better alternatives.

489
00:30:50,480 --> 00:30:56,080
Instead of saying, I need more money, you can say, I'd like to discuss my compensation.

490
00:30:56,080 --> 00:31:01,080
Or instead of, how much will you pay me in an interview, you can ask, what's the

491
00:31:01,080 --> 00:31:03,880
salary range for this position?

492
00:31:03,880 --> 00:31:06,800
These phrases sound calmer and more professional.

493
00:31:06,800 --> 00:31:10,480
You're opening a conversation, not making a demand.

494
00:31:10,480 --> 00:31:12,600
And notice the vocabulary.

495
00:31:12,600 --> 00:31:19,320
In professional settings, we often use words like salary, compensation, and package instead

496
00:31:19,320 --> 00:31:20,760
of just money.

497
00:31:20,760 --> 00:31:26,560
Yes, salary usually means a fixed amount you earn monthly or yearly.

498
00:31:26,560 --> 00:31:31,640
Compensation is even more professional because it includes salary plus benefits.

499
00:31:31,640 --> 00:31:36,560
That's why HR and managers often say compensation package.

500
00:31:36,560 --> 00:31:41,460
Now let's talk about asking for raise, because this is one of the hardest conversations for

501
00:31:41,460 --> 00:31:42,600
