518
00:32:38,400 --> 00:32:43,720
That sounds very professional, calm, clear, and focused on value.

519
00:32:43,720 --> 00:32:48,680
Notice I didn't say I want to raise. I said discuss my compensation.

520
00:32:48,680 --> 00:32:53,920
Exactly. Now let's quickly talk about some common mistakes learners make.

521
00:32:53,920 --> 00:32:57,120
One common mistake is saying expensive salary.

522
00:32:57,120 --> 00:32:59,380
We don't use expensive for salaries.

523
00:32:59,380 --> 00:33:03,080
We say high salary or competitive salary.

524
00:33:03,080 --> 00:33:06,440
Another mistake is saying, I gain a salary.

525
00:33:06,440 --> 00:33:08,760
In English, we earn or make money.

526
00:33:08,760 --> 00:33:10,400
We don't gain it.

527
00:33:10,400 --> 00:33:13,640
And a big one is confusing raise and promotion.

528
00:33:13,640 --> 00:33:15,440
A raise is more money.

529
00:33:15,440 --> 00:33:17,880
A promotion is a new position.

530
00:33:17,880 --> 00:33:20,760
Now let's do a quick practice for listeners.

531
00:33:20,760 --> 00:33:23,080
Try saying this sentence out loud.

532
00:33:23,080 --> 00:33:27,880
I'd like to discuss my compensation based on my recent performance.

533
00:33:27,880 --> 00:33:29,280
And now this one.

534
00:33:29,280 --> 00:33:32,300
Could you tell me the salary range for this role?

535
00:33:32,300 --> 00:33:36,740
If you can say those comfortably, you're already sounding professional.

536
00:33:36,740 --> 00:33:38,140
So let's wrap up.

537
00:33:38,140 --> 00:33:44,360
When talking about salary at work in English, avoid emotional or very direct language.

538
00:33:44,360 --> 00:33:49,820
Use professional words like compensation, salary range, and growth.

539
00:33:49,820 --> 00:33:54,620
on your value and contributions, not your personal financial needs.

540
00:33:54,620 --> 00:33:57,700
And remember, confidence comes from practice.

